<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
<!-- Gokwik theme code start -->
{%- comment -%}
  preconnect (not just dns-prefetch) for the GoKwik hosts.

  Why: snippets/gokwik.liquid loads merchant.integration.js with `defer`, and
  executeFlow() waits a maximum of 3s (waitForGoKwik) for the SDK before it
  gives up and does `window.location.href = "/checkout"` — a fallback order.
  dns-prefetch only resolves DNS; preconnect also completes the TCP + TLS
  handshake, which typically saves 100-300ms on mobile and widens the margin
  against that 3s budget.

  dns-prefetch lines are kept as a fallback for browsers without preconnect.
  No crossorigin: merchant.integration.js is a plain <script>, so a
  non-CORS connection is the one that actually gets reused.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://pdp.gokwik.co">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://api.gokwik.co">
<link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://pdp.gokwik.co/">
<link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://api.gokwik.co">
{% render 'gokwik' %}
<!-- Gokwik theme code End -->
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#1a1225">

  {%- comment -%}
    Collabloom and Skelecoll are reachable at BOTH /pages/<handle> (legacy) and
    /products/<handle> (where the nav, footer and sitemap now point). Both served
    ~18,000 words of the same content and each declared itself canonical, so
    Search Console reported "Duplicate, Google chose different canonical than
    user" and the ranking signals were split across two URLs. Point the legacy
    page at the product URL so they consolidate. A 301 redirect in admin is the
    better fix; this holds the line until that exists.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign dc_canonical = canonical_url -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'page' -%}
    {%- case page.handle -%}
      {%- when 'collabloom' -%}{%- assign dc_canonical = shop.url | append: '/products/collabloom' -%}
      {%- when 'skelecoll' -%}{%- assign dc_canonical = shop.url | append: '/products/skelecoll' -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ dc_canonical }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    Favicon. Without an icon link the browser falls back to requesting
    /favicon.ico at the domain root, which Shopify does not serve: that 404
    was the console error in Lighthouse's best-practices audit, and it left
    the store with a blank browser tab. A merchant-uploaded favicon still
    wins; the theme assets are the fallback when that setting is empty.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
  {%- else -%}
    <link rel="icon" href="{{ 'favicon.ico' | asset_url }}" sizes="any">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ 'favicon.png' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ 'apple-touch-icon.png' | asset_url }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ─── Journal SEO overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────
    Journal articles are theme files, not Shopify blog posts, so their
    title tag and meta description are defined here rather than in admin.
    Titles are kept under ~55 characters including the brand suffix, and
    descriptions around 105 characters, with the primary keyword first.

    Adding a weekly article? Add one `when` block below.
    (See JOURNAL-HOWTO.md at the repo root.)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign dc_title = page_title -%}
  {%- assign dc_desc = page_description -%}

  {%- if template.name == 'page' -%}
    {%- case page.handle -%}
      {%- when 'blog' or 'journal' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'The Dr Collagen Journal' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Evidence-led writing on collagen, skin and joints from the doctors who formulate Dr Collagen.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-for-skin' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen for Skin: Does It Work?' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Does collagen work for skin? A dermatologist on the trial evidence, the right dose, and a real timeline.' -%}
      {%- when 'glutathione-for-skin' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Glutathione for Skin: Benefits & Dose' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'What oral glutathione does for pigmentation, the 250mg dose trials used, and why IV is a different risk.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-for-joint-pain' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen for Joint Pain: The Evidence' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'An orthopaedic surgeon on the collagen joint trials, the 5-10g doses that worked, and vs glucosamine.' -%}
      {%- when 'supplements-for-knee-pain' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Supplements for Knee Pain: What Works' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = '11 knee pain supplements graded by trial evidence by an orthopaedic surgeon. What works, what does not.' -%}
      {%- when 'marine-vs-bovine-collagen' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Marine vs Bovine Collagen: Which Is Better?' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Marine vs bovine collagen, compared by a dermatologist: types, absorption, diet fit and cost per gram.' -%}
      {%- when 'marine-collagen' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Marine Collagen: Benefits, Dose and How to Choose' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Marine collagen, explained by a dermatologist: the dose trials used, the 2,000 Da rule, how to choose one.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-for-hair' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen for Hair: What It Can and Cannot Do' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen for hair: a dermatologist on where it helps, where it will not, and a realistic 3 to 6 month wait.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-for-women' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen for Women: What Changes by Decade' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen for women: what changes at 25, 35, 45 and after menopause, and what to look for at each stage.' -%}
      {%- when 'boost-collagen-naturally' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Boost Collagen Naturally: What Actually Works' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Boost collagen naturally: the vitamin C dose, the protein target Indian diets miss, and what UV undoes.' -%}
      {%- when 'types-of-collagen' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Types of Collagen: 1 vs 2 vs 3 Explained Simply' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Types of collagen explained by an orthopaedic surgeon: what type 1, 2 and 3 do, and which one you need.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-for-men' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen for Men: Joints, Recovery and Skin' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen for men: an orthopaedic surgeon on the pre-training tendon dose, joints, and what it cannot do.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-tablets-vs-shots' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen Tablets vs Capsules vs Shots: Honest Guide' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen tablets hold under 1g, but the trials used 5g to 10g. A surgeon compares all five formats.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-peptides' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen Peptides: What They Are and How They Work' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen peptides explained: why hydrolysis matters, how Pro-Hyp signals cells, and the real dose.' -%}
      {%- when 'collagen-vs-whey-protein' -%}
        {%- assign dc_title = 'Collagen vs Whey Protein: What Each One Is For' -%}
        {%- assign dc_desc = 'Collagen vs whey protein: whey builds muscle, collagen feeds tendon and cartilage. A surgeon explains.' -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <title>
    {{ dc_title }}
    {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; tagged "{{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}"{% endif -%}
    {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
    {%- unless dc_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
  </title>

  {%- if dc_desc != blank -%}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ dc_desc | escape }}">
  {%- else -%}
    <meta name="description" content="Japanese marine collagen, micro-hydrolysed to under 2,000 Daltons and stacked with the co-factors collagen synthesis needs. Four formulas for skin, joints, body composition, and gut.">
  {%- endif -%}

  <!-- Open Graph -->
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name }}">
  <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
  <meta property="og:title" content="{{ dc_title | escape }}">
  {%- if dc_desc != blank -%}
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ dc_desc | escape }}">
  {%- else -%}
    <meta property="og:description" content="Japanese marine collagen, micro-hydrolysed to under 2,000 Daltons. Four formulas for skin, joints, body composition, and gut.">
  {%- endif -%}
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  {%- if settings.og_image != blank -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ settings.og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ settings.og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <!-- Fonts: Playfair Display + DM Sans — trimmed from 13 weights to 8.
       Enough to preserve the existing homepage/product weights (300-700)
       while removing the redundant italic + 600 mid-bolds. -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  {%- comment -%}
    Loaded off the critical path. As a plain <link rel="stylesheet"> to a
    third-party origin this cost ~750ms of render-blocking time for 1.5KB:
    almost all of it the DNS + TLS + request round trip, not the download.

    media="print" makes the browser fetch it at low priority without blocking
    render; onload flips it to media="all" and it applies normally. Safe here
    only because the 'Playfair Fallback' / 'DM Sans Fallback' faces below are
    metric-matched with size-adjust, so the swap does not reflow - that was
    worth 0.515 CLS on the Collabloom page before those were added. Keep the
    fallbacks in sync with this if the font stack ever changes.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="preload" as="style" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&display=swap">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&display=swap" media="print" onload="this.media='all';this.onload=null">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&display=swap"></noscript>

  <style>
    /* ── Metric-matched font fallbacks (CLS) ─────────────────────────────
       Google Fonts load with display=swap, so Georgia/system paints first
       and Playfair/DM Sans replace it ~450ms later. Measured in-browser,
       Playfair renders 1.0107x the width of Georgia and DM Sans 1.0102x
       Arial. That ~1% is small, but .hero-title is clamp(52px,7vw,96px) —
       enough to change where the heading wraps, and one extra line moved
       everything below it. That single reflow measured 0.515 CLS on the
       Collabloom product page (Google's threshold is 0.1).

       size-adjust scales the fallback so it occupies the same width as the
       real font. The swap then happens without reflowing. Ratios come from
       measurement, not estimation — re-measure if the fonts ever change. */
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'Playfair Fallback';
      src: local('Georgia'), local('Times New Roman');
      size-adjust: 101.07%;
      ascent-override: 105%;
      descent-override: 21%;
      line-gap-override: 0%;
    }
    @font-face {
      font-family: 'DM Sans Fallback';
      src: local('Arial'), local('Helvetica Neue');
      size-adjust: 101.02%;
      ascent-override: 100%;
      descent-override: 24%;
      line-gap-override: 0%;
    }
  </style>

  {%- comment -%}
    Preload the first hero frame on the homepage for fast LCP — desktop only.
    #scroll-hero is display:none under 768px, so on phones this was preloading
    361KB that nothing ever painted. `media` scopes the preload to viewports
    that actually render the canvas animation.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" media="(min-width: 769px)" href="{{ 'hero-frame-0001.webp' | asset_url }}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The mobile hero is the LCP element. It lives inside .m-module, which is
      display:none above 768px, so it only ever renders on a phone — one
      candidate (800w) is enough and the preload can point straight at it.
      Do not add a 1200w candidate to that <img> without updating this hint:
      a preload that resolves to a different file than the renderer picks
      costs one wasted download and delays LCP by ~1s on a 4G connection.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" media="(max-width: 768px)" href="{{ 'hero-frame-0003-w800.webp' | asset_url }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <!-- Shared luxury theme system -->
  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <!-- Motion One - deferred. It used to load synchronously here because the
       homepage and product snippets destructure `Motion` in inline scripts,
       and a bare `defer` made those throw ReferenceError. Those five blocks
       are now gated on DOMContentLoaded, which deferred scripts are
       guaranteed to run before, so `defer` is safe. As a parser-blocking
       script this was the single largest render-blocking item on the site
       (~1.2s per PageSpeed). Self-hosted rather than CDN so it reuses the
       connection that already delivered the document.
       If you re-add a bare `Motion` reference to an inline script, gate it on
       DOMContentLoaded too - do not remove `defer` to make it work. -->
  <script src="{{ 'motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

  <!-- Shared luxury runtime — safe to defer, only listens for DOMContentLoaded -->
  <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

  {{ content_for_header }}
</head>
<body class="template-{{ template.name | handle }}{% if template.suffix %} template-{{ template.name | handle }}--{{ template.suffix | handle }}{% endif %}">

  <a class="skip-to-content" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  {%- comment -%}
    Pages with their own per-page nav + film-grain + particles + cursor:
    the homepage and the four flagship product landing pages. We skip
    rendering the global header/footer AND the global cinematic chrome
    on those, so layers don't double up.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign has_inline_nav = false -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'index' -%}{%- assign has_inline_nav = true -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'page' -%}
    {%- case page.handle -%}
      {%- when 'collabloom' or 'skelecoll' or 'collatrim' or 'metastable' -%}
        {%- assign has_inline_nav = true -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%} Flagship products now render their landing snippet (with its own
     nav) via templates/product.liquid — skip the global header/footer there too. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
    {%- case product.handle -%}
      {%- when 'collabloom' or 'skelecoll' or 'collatrim' or 'metastable' -%}
        {%- assign has_inline_nav = true -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- unless has_inline_nav -%}
    {%- comment -%} Global cinematic chrome for fallback pages {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="dc-film-grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="dc-vignette" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <canvas class="dc-particles" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

    {% section 'header' %}
  {%- endunless -%}

  <main id="main" role="main">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- unless has_inline_nav -%}
    {% section 'footer' %}
  {%- endunless -%}

  <button class="dc-back-to-top" aria-label="Back to top" type="button">
    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
      <line x1="12" y1="19" x2="12" y2="5"></line>
      <polyline points="5 12 12 5 19 12"></polyline>
    </svg>
  </button>

</body>
</html>
